aived by the Cardinals on August 27, 2024.\n\nDETROIT LIONS (SECOND STINT)\nOn August 28, 2024, the Detroit Lions claimed Nowaske off waivers. On October 27 against the Tennessee Titans, Nowaske recorded his first interception off of Mason Rudolph.\nOn March 14, 2025, Nowaske re-signed with the Lions.\nOn March 16, 2026, Nowaske re-signed with the Lions."}],"wikidataId":"Q121461325","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-03-13","text":"Signed DB Izien Christian and LB Trevor Nowaske to contracts."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/5144894","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/N/NowaTr00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/trevor-nowaske/169859","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/trevor-nowaske/11481","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevor_Nowaske"},"insights":["Ranks 1st of 80 qualified linebackers in completion % allowed.","Ranks 2nd of 80 qualified linebackers in passer rating allowed.","On the field for 28% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.4M is the 30th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season."]}